    isbefore: []  # e7b5
    duplicate_of: []  # e7b5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e7b5
    pr_ref:  # e7b5
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family F). Stand-alone finding F23.3 previously folded onto INV-luhur. Full evidence remains on INV-luhur's pass-23 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`profile.languages` and `metrics.languages` carry disjoint language sets, with symmetric difference of 4 across two writers.\n\n- `profile.languages` includes `xml`, `yaml`, etc.\n- `metrics.languages` includes `ansible`, `unknown`, etc.\n\nThe yaml/ansible mismatch suggests one writer reclassifies YAML files as Ansible when they parse as playbooks; the other doesn't. The `unknown` entry in metrics (23 edges, 0 nodes, 0 files) means metrics rolled up edges whose src language couldn't be classified — profile, walking files directly, never sees this category.\n\nTwo writers (`profile.compute_profile` and `metrics.compute_metrics`) disagree on the language set. Closely related to WI-jikik schema-consolidation gap: profile.languages has `{files, loc}` per language; metrics.languages has `{nodes, edges}` per language — fields are complementary, but the SETS are also disjoint.\n\nPass-25 F25.13 / F25.15 catalogue related \"two analyzer cohorts, two surfaces\" pattern (markdown/yaml analyzers feed centrality_scores; source-language analyzers feed nodes[]). This row is the language-vocabulary instance of that pattern.\n\n## Invariant\n\n`set(profile.languages.keys()) == set(metrics.languages.keys())` — and ideally, both consult the same canonical language-classifier so the symmetric difference is structurally impossible.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nTwo paths:\n\n**(a) Unify the two writers** on a shared language-classifier (same path-pattern + content-sniff logic). Removes the disjunction structurally.\n\n**(b) Cross-link the writers** so each emits BOTH `{files, loc, nodes, edges}` for the union of languages observed. Larger payload but each writer is independently consistent.\n\nThe fold-audit lists this row alongside WI-metrics-languages-files-empty (which is a per-language-FILE gap on the metrics side); both fixes likely share an implementation site.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F23.3** — INV-luhur discussion entry 2026-06-02T04:37:45 (pass-23 batch; paragraph beginning \"(F23.3) profile.languages and metrics.languages carry disjoint language sets\").\n- Cousin pass-25 F25.13 grammar-naming asymmetry (`language_pack:*` vs `tree-sitter-*`) — same shape, different surface.\n\nLab notebooks: passes 23, 25 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-luhur**.\n- Sibling: **WI-metrics-languages-files-empty** (Family F — per-language file count on metrics; shared fix-site).\n- Sibling: **INV-mozaf** (per-language file accounting gap — global level).\n- Sibling: **WI-jikik** (schema-consolidation between profile.languages and metrics.languages).\n- Family F siblings."  # e7b5
    fields: {}  # e7b5
- op: discuss  # be3d
